From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:44:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/74] MIPS: ingenic: XBurst II has a physically tagged icache

The Ingenic CPU support treats every XBurst instruction cache as
virtually tagged: the feature overrides, written for the first XBurst
SoCs, fix cpu_has_vtag_icache to 1, and the probe marks the icache so.
That holds for XBurst1, but not for the XBurst II core of the X2600,
whose icache Ingenic's own kernel treats as physically tagged (its
X2600 feature overrides set cpu_has_vtag_icache to 0). With a virtually
tagged icache assumed, the kernel flushes it where this core does not
need it, on context switches among others.

Mark the icache virtually tagged on XBurst1 only, and let the flag
decide instead of the override. On the X2600 a pipe round trip between
two processes (two context switches) takes 3% less: 16.4 instead of
17.0 us. 2400 fork + exec runs alternating between two programs at the
same addresses all ran the right one.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h | 1 -
 arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c                               | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
index 08d6e2349..cbcaf7b17 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/mach-ingenic/cpu-feature-overrides.h
@@ -27,7 +27,6 @@
 #define cpu_has_mips3d 0
 #define cpu_has_smartmips 0
 #define kernel_uses_llsc	1
-#define cpu_has_vtag_icache	1
 #define cpu_has_dc_aliases	0
 #define cpu_has_ic_fills_f_dc	0
 #define cpu_has_pindexed_dcache 0
diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
index b976ef5cc..f8e654e82 100644
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -1769,8 +1769,9 @@ static inline void cpu_probe_ingenic(struct cpuinfo_mips *c, unsigned int cpu)
 	c->options &= ~MIPS_CPU_COUNTER;
 	BUG_ON(__builtin_constant_p(cpu_has_counter) && cpu_has_counter);
 
-	/* XBurst has virtually tagged icache */
-	c->icache.flags |= MIPS_CACHE_VTAG;
+	/* XBurst1 has a virtually tagged icache, XBurst II does not */
+	if ((c->processor_id & PRID_IMP_MASK) != PRID_IMP_XBURST2)
+		c->icache.flags |= MIPS_CACHE_VTAG;
 
 	switch (c->processor_id & PRID_IMP_MASK) {
 
